  "changes": [
    "R1: file-only authority shared by iOS source/read/exists/getSize/getPath; isDirectory/bookmarks/staging reject non-file URLs while original name/URI metadata remains available.",
    "R2: saver transfers staging ownership then revalidates attached visible active-scene idle presenter and ancestors on Main after IO, immediately before native presentation.",
    "R3: separate presentation phases, result claim, provider completion and native dismissal; cancellation suppresses callbacks/cancels work without early native-resource deletion; owner/callback await teardown.",
    "Native adaptive dismissal lifetime event is independent of the result guard; rejected/unstarted presentations clean, while accepted consumers retain resources through completion."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "New methods test Foundation files/NSURL and manually driven production-session policy, not presentIosDialog with an actual attached UIKit host.",
    "Immediate post-present rejection detection requires a real normal-acceptance/rejection test; UIKit phase-property semantics were not executed here.",
    "Actual competing presenter during delayed staging, animated disposal, export provider consumption, interactive rollback and absent/refused transition coordinator remain native gates.",
    "No timer early-cleanup workaround: if UIKit never supplies either accepted-dismissal completion or adaptive didDismiss, ownership can remain retained.",
    "No Gradle, Kotlin compiler, Apple linking, simulator, device or GUI run was performed for this correction."
  ]
